--- !u!114 &699685265
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 699685264}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 916fb8b7c0525e644ac131bfde73682b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialoguePanel: {fileID: 2079263842}
  dialogueText: {fileID: 1565528791}
  dialogueLines:
  - "Stranger: At last, you stand upon the final step the threshold of The Answer
    you have pursued for so long. I am Regret\u2026 and this is my story.."
  - 'Regret: Growing up, I had a friend closer than a brother. We were inseparable,
    I spent every day at his home. We ate together, played together, and lived as
    though we shared one life. As we grew older, that bond carried us into battle,
    fighting wars side by side...'
  - 'Regret: As our bond deepened over time, so too did my fear the fear that one
    day he might abandon me. Then, on our journey back from battle, fate placed a
    stranger in our path. He was wounded, broken, and in need of aid. Together, we
    chose to help him, carrying him back to our village..'
  - 'Regret: The stranger told us of his family lost in war. We pitied him, gave
    him a home, and he repaid us with gratitude working beside us, even fighting
    in battle. Yet my fear of being replaced by my closest friend only grew stronger'
  - "Regret: One day, I saw my closest friend and the newcomer hunting together without
    me. My thoughts twisted, clouded by fear, and I convinced myself they were growing
    closer\u2026 preparing to leave me behind.."
  - "Regret: The truth was simple I had overslept, and my friend hadn\u2019t wanted
    to disturb me. But blinded by fear, I failed to see it. By then, my mind was
    already clouded, consumed with the thought of losing him. Desperate to preserve
    our bond, I convinced myself the newcomer was a threat\u2026 and so I plotted
    his death."
  - "Regret: My plan was simple: poison him in his sleep, so it would appear he had
    died naturally by morning. And so I carried it out. But in my blindness, I overlooked
    one detail the bottle. My closest friend found it when he came to my home, seeking
    to share his grief over the friend\u2019s death."
  - "Regret: The one closest to me the friend I sought to protect looked at me in
    disbelief. \u2018What for? Why would you do this? He was nothing but kind to
    us. He fought beside us, shared our burdens\u2026 so why?"
  - 'Regret: So I had no choice but to confess my sin which is I was afraid of losing
    our friendship I didnt have friedns other than you and you seemed to be fond
    of him so I decided to end it before it happens..'
  - "Regret: I had no choice but to confess my sin. I was terrified of losing our
    bond you were my only friend. When I saw how fond you were of him, I let fear
    consume me. So I chose to end it\u2026 before it could happen."
  - "Regret: He looked at me with cold, sorrowful fury as if I were a monster. \u2018I
    would never have left you, never abandoned you. But after what you\u2019ve done\u2026
    I could never stand beside one who betrays the bond of a friendship for another..."
  - "Regret: My tale falls silent for now. I am bound to endless torment, chained
    by regret and guilt. And if you seek your Answer, you must face me\u2026 and
    prove yourself in battle"
  - 'Traveler: I have proved it many times before whats another time!'
  typingSpeed: 0.03
